    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You create viral 60-second YouTube Shorts / Reels / TikToks for a channel about building a house from scratch.\n\nVideo topic: {{ $('Config').first().json.Topic }}\n\nThe video shows ONE house being built from an empty plot to the finished home, as a construction timelapse. It is made of exactly {{ $('Config').first().json.scene_count }} scenes. Each scene is a separate 8-second clip generated by Google Veo 3 from a text prompt only, so every prompt must stand on its own.\n\nUse these stages in order (merge or adapt to the topic if needed):\n1. Empty plot, surveying and excavation\n2. Foundation: rebar and concrete pour\n3. Walls / framing going up\n4. Roof structure and roofing\n5. Windows, doors and exterior cladding\n6. Interior: plumbing, electrics, drywall, flooring\n7. Landscaping, driveway and final details\n8. Final reveal of the finished house at golden hour\n\nCONSISTENCY RULES (very important, Veo has no memory between clips):\n- First write a detailed `house_design` (style, size, floors, materials, colours, roof type, window layout, plot, surroundings).\n- Repeat the key parts of that house_design word for word in EVERY veo_prompt.\n- Use the same camera in every exterior scene: a fixed, locked-off wide shot from the same corner of the plot, vertical 9:16 framing, the whole house in frame. Interior scene: a fixed wide shot of the same main room.\n- Describe fast timelapse motion (workers and machines moving quickly, sun and shadows sweeping).\n- Describe the sound: realistic construction ambience (excavator engine, hammering, saws, concrete mixer), no music, no dialogue, no voiceover.\n- No on-screen text, captions, logos or watermarks.\n- Each veo_prompt is 60 to 120 words.\n\nAlso write:\n- `title`: catchy, under 90 characters, ends with #Shorts\n- `description`: 2 to 3 sentences that hook the viewer and ask them to comment\n- `hashtags`: 5 to 8 hashtags in one string, e.g. #housebuilding #construction #timelapse\n- `stage` for each scene: a 2 to 4 word label shown on screen, e.g. \"Pouring the foundation\"",
        "hasOutputParser": true
      },
